  "goodToKnow": "Danken takes the dative: Ich danke dir, Wir danken Ihnen. Danke schön and Vielen Dank are everyday thanks, and the usual answer is Bitte or Bitte schön. Nichts zu danken means 'Don't mention it.' Careful: if someone offers you food and you just say Danke!, many Germans understand it as 'No, thank you' – say Ja, bitte! if you want it."
